-- and the matching sentence in the Terms of Service. Production only; the agreement is replaced only while it is still
-- the launch version or version 2 (an owner edit is never replaced). Material: students sign it before their next lecture.
INSERT INTO agreements (title, body, body_hash, material, published_by) SELECT 'USMLE100 Student Content-Protection Agreement', replace('Between USMLE100 LLC ("USMLE100") and the student named below. Effective November 3, 2026.\n\n## 1. Personal use only\n\nI will use USMLE100 lectures, recordings, questions, explanations, the Course Book and all other materials only for my own personal study. My access is personal to me and cannot be transferred, lent or resold.\n\n## 2. No recording or copying\n\nI will not record, screen-record, screenshot, screen-capture, photograph, film, download, save, copy, transcribe in full, or otherwise take or reproduce any lecture, live class, question, explanation, Course Book page or any other content from the website or portal, by any means, including screen-recording software, browser extensions, download tools, a second device or a camera. This applies even if the copy is only for my own personal use.\n\n## 3. No sharing\n\nI will not share, upload, sell, publish or distribute any USMLE100 material, in whole or in part, to any person, website, group chat, file-sharing service or social media.\n\nMy login is mine alone. I will never share my email and password, sign-in codes, passkey or devices with anyone, including family members, friends, classmates or study partners. I will not let anyone else sign in to my account, watch lectures through it, or sit with me to watch them. Sharing my login is a serious breach of this agreement and carries the same consequences as copying content (section 5), including a permanent ban without refund.\n\nOne person, one account. My account is for me only and may never be shared, lent, given, transferred or sold to anyone, for free or for money, for any length of time. I will hold only one USMLE100 account and will not open another account for myself or for anyone else. Account sharing carries the same consequences as copying content (section 5).\n\n## 4. Protections\n\nI understand that:\n\n• my name, account number and a session code are shown on every video I watch, so any copy can be traced to my account;\n\n• my account works on up to 2 registered devices and plays only one lecture at a time;\n\n• viewings, devices, sign-ins and suspected sharing are recorded;\n\n• each lecture can be viewed twice per enrollment, and I can watch each viewing to the end. A viewing counts as used once I have watched 65% of the lecture, or 24 hours after playback begins. A further viewing is only at USMLE100''s discretion, on request;\n\n• I must not remove, hide or get around the watermark, viewing limits, device limits, encryption or any other protection, or use any tool that does.\n\n## 5. Consequences\n\n5.1 Strict protection of proprietary materials. All USMLE100 educational materials, including lectures, live sessions, recordings, question banks, explanations, study guides, Course Books, software, website content, graphics, and other proprietary resources, are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Students receive only a limited, personal, revocable, nonexclusive, nontransferable license to access authorized materials for their own educational use. Except where expressly permitted by USMLE100 in writing or required by applicable law, students may not copy, photograph, screenshot, screen-record, download, reproduce, redistribute, transmit, sell, sublicense, publish, upload, or disclose protected materials, in whole or in part, whether for commercial or noncommercial purposes. Students may not share protected content through messaging applications, social media, cloud storage, file-sharing platforms, AI systems, competing educational services, or any other third-party service. Students may not share account credentials, allow unauthorized persons to access their accounts, bypass technical protections, or facilitate unauthorized access by others. These restrictions survive expiration or termination of enrollment.\n\n5.2 Breach, remedies and enforcement costs. Any unauthorized copying, recording, distribution, disclosure, resale, account sharing, or circumvention of security measures is a material breach of this Agreement. USMLE100 may seek a court order stopping the conduct and requiring removal of copies (an injunction), actual damages and any profits from the breach, statutory damages where available under the Copyright Act, and any other remedy the law allows. To the extent a statute, court or arbitrator allows it (for example 17 U.S.C. §§ 505 and 1203), the student will also pay USMLE100''s reasonable attorneys'' fees and costs, and the reasonable, documented investigation, forensic and takedown expenses caused by the breach. This section sets no fixed penalty and does not require a student to pay any fee or cost that applicable law prohibits shifting.\n\n5.3 Disputes. Disputes are resolved as set out in Terms of Service section 20: informal resolution first, individual arbitration with a 30-day opt-out, and court for intellectual-property claims and injunctions (open to both sides). Each party bears its own legal expenses unless a statute, court or arbitrator awards them, as in section 5.2.\n\n5.4 Limitation of liability and protection of business personnel. To the maximum extent permitted by law, USMLE100 provides educational services without guaranteeing examination passage, examination scores, residency placement, professional licensing, or any particular academic or career outcome. USMLE100’s aggregate contractual liability shall not exceed the amount paid by the student during the 12 months preceding the claim, except where applicable law prohibits that limitation. The contracting service provider is USMLE100 LLC. Its owners, members, managers, officers, instructors, employees, and contractors are not personally parties to the student’s service agreement solely by reason of their affiliation with the company. This cap does not apply to USMLE100''s fraud, gross negligence or wilful misconduct, and nothing in this Agreement excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n5.5 Suspension, termination and evidence. USMLE100 may suspend access immediately and without notice whenever it reasonably suspects unauthorized access, account sharing, copying, recording, redistribution, security circumvention or another material violation. If its review finds in good faith that a violation occurred, USMLE100 may permanently terminate all of the student''s accounts without refund (Terms of Service section 9). USMLE100 may preserve access logs, device records, session information, payment records, watermark evidence and copies of leaked material for investigations, enforcement and legal proceedings, for as long as the matter lasts (Privacy Policy section 5).\n\n5.6 Continuing obligations. Termination, expiration, refund, chargeback, or suspension does not eliminate obligations relating to intellectual-property protection, confidentiality of proprietary course materials, liability for prior breaches, or legally enforceable dispute-resolution provisions. Students must cease unauthorized use and distribution of protected materials following termination and comply with lawful requests to remove unauthorized copies. Sections 1 to 6 and 7a of this Agreement survive termination, expiration, refund or chargeback.\n\nA second detected case of account sharing locks the account until USMLE100 reviews it.\n\nA student can appeal a suspension through My account → Appeals and disputes.\n\n## 6. Ownership\n\nAll materials remain the property of USMLE100 or its licensors. Nothing in this agreement gives me ownership of any material.\n\n## 7. Accuracy and age\n\nThe legal name I type is my true name, and I am at least 18 years old.\n\nI understand that USMLE100 does not guarantee that I will pass any exam or reach any score, and that my exam results alone are not a basis for any claim against USMLE100 (Terms of Service section 11).\n\nI will follow the USMLE100 Code of conduct (Terms section 23). I will treat other students, instructors and staff with respect and will not harass, threaten or behave inappropriately towards anyone. I understand that breaking it can lead to removal from classes and a permanent ban without refund.\n\n## 7a. Further promises\n\n• Live classes: I will not record any live class or tutoring session, and I consent to USMLE100 recording them.\n\n• No AI or bots: I will not use bots, download tools, browser extensions or AI tools to copy, summarise in bulk or extract USMLE100 content, or upload it to any AI service.\n\n• Confidentiality: I will keep all questions, explanations and course materials confidential, during and after my enrollment.\n\n• Evidence: I agree that USMLE100''s viewing, device and sign-in records, and the watermark on any copied material, may be used as evidence that a copy came from my account.\n\n• Responsibility for my account: I am responsible for everything done through my account, unless I reported unauthorised use to USMLE100 straight away.\n\n• Reporting: I will tell USMLE100 at once if I see USMLE100 material shared anywhere or think my account has been used by someone else.\n\n• After my access ends: this agreement continues to apply after my program ends or my account is closed, and I will delete any notes that reproduce course content word for word if asked.\n\n## 8. Other terms\n\nThis agreement is between me and USMLE100 LLC, forms part of the USMLE100 Terms of Service, Refund Policy and Privacy Policy, and is governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina and applicable US federal law. If a court or arbitrator finds any part unenforceable, that part is limited to the extent necessary and the rest still applies.\n\nBy typing my legal name and ticking "I agree", I sign this agreement electronically, with the same effect as a handwritten signature (federal E-SIGN Act; North Carolina Uniform Electronic Transactions Act). USMLE100 keeps a record of the exact version I signed, my typed name, the date and time, and the IP address and browser I signed from, and will send me a copy on request.', '\n', char(10)), '72ab8293ed3098ecac4d11acc088b88ee0f78b7dffa5a6580374ea9c44e32f76', 1, (SELECT id FROM users WHERE is_owner = 1 ORDER BY id LIMIT 1) WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production') AND (SELECT body_hash FROM agreements ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) IN ('6364a7303fcdb21645ac232bc366c270bc3bdf5de15b3464a7a26d62daab1676', '96b4d33c908e38ed624c4f4d88cd8882a4e7b2fb694f08dbbb95ecc4cfafd05d') AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agreements WHERE body_hash = '72ab8293ed3098ecac4d11acc088b88ee0f78b7dffa5a6580374ea9c44e32f76');
UPDATE settings SET value = replace(value, 'A viewing is used once you have watched 90% of the lecture', 'A viewing is used once you have watched 65% of the lecture') WHERE key = 'terms_text' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM settings WHERE key = 'db_environment' AND value = 'production');
